# pick: arm A takes its tweezers at its rack, lifts the DIP-8 out of
# the tray and puts it in the vise on the turntable, which holds it when
# A lets go; the turntable turns the DIP a quarter round. A picks the
# LED and holds it up; the vise opens and the DIP, held by nothing,
# falls to the floor and is lost, and so does the LED when A lets go.
reset circuit=demo
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-24 rpy=0,0,90
vise close
release A U1
lift A mm=60
stage turn=90
pick A D1 grasp=body
move A to=60,0,80
vise open
release A D1
